GreenBoost third_party/turboquant — vendored third-party code
===============================================================

Upstream project: turboquant
Repository:       https://github.com/OmarHory/turboquant
Upstream commit:  ecf3f21031d63d2624b57bc91f382ce5acc2c011 (2026-03-29)
License:          MIT License (see LICENSE, verbatim from upstream)
Import date:      2026-07-26

Paper: Zandieh et al., "TurboQuant: Online Vector Quantization with
Near-optimal Distortion Rate", arXiv:2504.19874 (ICLR 2026).

This is a SEPARATE implementation from `gb_quant_tq.py`'s existing
TurboQuant weight-quantization codebooks (own workbench, no upstream repo
tracked) — this vendored tree specifically covers the KV-CACHE / attention
side (`QuantizedAttention`, `TurboQuantCache`), which `gb_attn.py` did not
previously have: `gb_attn.py`'s own TurboQuant support quantizes K/V then
DEQUANTIZES before calling SDPA (bandwidth saving only, no packed storage,
no real memory saving). This vendored tree adds `QuantizedAttention` (runs
Q·Kᵀ directly on compressed indices, no dequantization) and true 2/3/4-bit
byte packing (`packing.py`) , real KV memory compression, not just
bandwidth reduction.

What was imported
------------------
`turboquant/` (`__init__.py`, `core.py`, `cache.py`, `packing.py`,
`attention.py`, `cuda_kernels.py` , the whole package, only 6 files/1698
lines total, genuinely small and self-contained unlike auto_round's
139-file closure), `LICENSE` — verbatim from upstream.

NOT vendored: `benchmarks/`, `scripts/`, `results/`, `assets/`,
`.env.example` (upstream's own benchmark/paper-reproduction tooling) ,
this repo's own tests (tests/test_gb_attn_packed.py) cover the
GreenBoost-side integration, same exclusion policy as every other
third_party/*/NOTICE in this repo.

New runtime dependency (declared in synapse_engine/pyproject.toml):
`scipy` (`cache.py`/`core.py`/`cuda_kernels.py` use `scipy.stats.norm` for
the Lloyd-Max Gaussian quantizer construction). `transformers.cache_utils.
DynamicCache`/`DynamicLayer` (used by `cache.py`) were already a direct
dependency.

Consumer: `gb_attn.py`'s `patch_sdpa(backend="packed")` (opt-in,
`GB_ATTN_BACKEND=packed`; default `"dequant"` unchanged) — torch-engine/
fallback/diffusion attention only, NOT gb-synapse's llama.cpp path
(llama.cpp owns its own KV cache and never calls
`F.scaled_dot_product_attention`; its equivalent lever is
`--cache-type-k/v` via `_pick_kv_type`, a separate mechanism — see
gb_attn.py's own module docstring).

This tree is a verbatim copy at the pinned commit , no local patches. If one
is ever needed, add a "Local modifications" section here (bulleted, in
order) per the convention established in third_party/gemlite/NOTICE and
third_party/auto_round/NOTICE.
